.TH "daharness\-repl" "1" "" ""
.SH NAME
daharness\-repl \(em operator REPL and one\-shot lane for the daharness
framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]daharness\-repl\f[R] [\f[I]run|search|scope|engagement\f[R] ...]
\f[B]daharness\-repl\f[R] \f[B]run\f[R] \f[I]tool_id\f[R]
[\f[I]\-\-flag\f[R] \f[I]value\f[R] ...]
\(em one\-shot exit
.SH DESCRIPTION
The operator seat (also \f[I]tool_repl.py\f[R], which keeps its filename
\(em kernelspec argv, systemd unit and refresh stubs depend on it).
The operator chooses and invokes tools directly \(em there is no LLM in
this lane and no approval gate, because the operator \f[B]is\f[R] the
approval.
.PP
Interactive commands and modes:
.TP
\f[B]run\f[R] \f[I]tool_id\f[R] [\f[I]\-\-flag\f[R] \f[I]value\f[R] ...]
Execute a tool; flags follow its manifest parameter schema.
.TP
\f[B]search\f[R] \f[I]query\f[R]
Semantic search over the tool registry (candidate manifests, no
execution).
.TP
\f[B]reindex\f[R]
Refresh tool \f[I]manifests\f[R] only.
Semantic embeddings stay stale until the full index rebuild
(\f[CR]python \-m daharness.core\f[R]); restart the Brain after.
.TP
\f[B]scope\f[R] \f[B]on\f[R]|\f[B]off\f[R] \f[I]handle\f[R]
Arm the scope gate for a target handle \(em the ONLY arming surface; the
state is never togglable by the LLM.
See \f[B]daharness\-safety(7)\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]engagement\f[R] \f[B]on\f[R]|\f[B]off\f[R] \f[I]slug\f[R]
Arm the engagement cobweb key that ties journal, evidence and findings
rows together; arming is deliberately REPL\-only.
See \f[B]daharness\-safety(7)\f[R].
